  "source_changes_reviewed": [
    "The 27,752-scalar full-string alphabet contains ASCII, unified Han ranges and the explicit punctuation set. Any other scalar takes the old whole-string normalization/deletion path.",
    "Native str and original normalize/category/camel/strip object guards avoid applying the identity certificate to changed hooks or str subclasses; unrecognized Unicode database versions fall back.",
    "Admitted scalars are individually NFKC/NFKD identities with combining class0 and no Mn deletion, and casefold stays inside the alphabet. Camel separation inserts ASCII spaces. The admitted set excludes composition marks and Hangul Jamo, preventing the relevant cross-character recomposition/reordering.",
    "This is an alphabet-relative argument. A normalized scalar alone does not prove arbitrary concatenation safe, and ASCII letters are not universally stable against arbitrary following combining marks.",
    "Canonical spelling, query phrase removal, identifier separation, stop-word behavior, indexed FTS values, source references and response packing are otherwise unchanged."
  ],
